  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Current satellite water vapor imagery \nshows a Pacific low advecting moisture into central Nevada. This \nmoisture is expected to facilitate thunderstorm development within\nthe next few hours, with storms expected to expand into eastern \nElko County overnight. Storms persist until late tomorrow \nafternoon, by which point the low will have traveled far enough \neast to cut off moisture over Nevada. Rainfall accumulation looks \nvery hit or miss at this time but the stronger storms are expected\nto produce around a tenth of an inch of rain along their path. \nCloud cover with these storms is also expected to limit high \ntemperatures tomorrow, with Humboldt County seeing highs around 80\nwhile more eastern locations will be limited to the lower 70s. \nFair weather is expected for the second half of the week, with dry\nconditions and highs returning to the low 80s across the area. A \nnew upper level trough is expected to clip the area for Friday and\nSaturday. No precipitation is currently expected with this \nsystem, however winds will increase and temperatures decrease. \nCool and breezy conditions are expected to continue to start next \nweek.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in showers and\nthunderstorms through tomorrow. Confidence remains moderate for\nrainfall totals. High confidence in fair weather through the end\nof the week. No changes to NBM output.",
